44:47.051 --> 44:56.598
[SPEAKER_01]: inside these people usually don't see but there's a lot of hours just how to optimize all these holes inside in the ribs and everywhere a lot of

44:56.678 --> 45:07.205
[SPEAKER_01]: work when you design the wing here so this yeah so this basically this and also new riser system yeah with pc which run really smoothly over the

45:07.245 --> 45:17.533
[SPEAKER_01]: police and yeah this is basically I want to talk a little bit about the internal structure of a wing because a lot of brands stress on this. The

45:17.593 --> 45:25.056
[SPEAKER_00]: internal structure is all about distributing air and maintaining the pressure in the canopy. Is that correct? Firstly, internal

45:25.116 --> 45:36.885
[SPEAKER_01]: construction is giving shape to the wing. So it's transferring pilot loads from the lines to the canopy. And as all we know, we have supported

45:36.985 --> 45:47.410
[SPEAKER_01]: ribs and unsupported ribs. So supported ribs is where the lines are connected to the rib. And this force then is distributed from the bottom

45:47.610 --> 45:57.999
[SPEAKER_01]: where the line is connected to the top where most of the lift is produced. So it's all about how these forces are distributing and according to

45:58.039 --> 46:10.225
[SPEAKER_01]: this force vector curve they go. you play how you put the cross holes in the ribs. So in the load, speaking about loading ribs now, so the ribs

46:10.265 --> 46:19.692
[SPEAKER_01]: which have lines connected. If a line is connected, then the vector goes of the force to the top surface in some conical shape. And so in between

46:19.732 --> 46:30.349
[SPEAKER_01]: this, you need to place the holes that you don't make deformation in the ribs. So how you place the holes is really important. How you place it in

46:30.389 --> 46:40.151
[SPEAKER_01]: the supported rips. Unsupported rips are the rips which have no line connections. These rips are just carrying the pure ram air pressure

46:40.211 --> 46:48.933
[SPEAKER_01]: inside. So we have ram air pressure and the canopy without rips will go to the board in physics. So all these rips are carrying, unloaded rips are

46:48.973 --> 46:57.695
[SPEAKER_01]: carrying just these pressure loads. so this you can play again with different shapes of the cross holes inside so it's all about this

46:58.035 --> 47:07.497
[SPEAKER_01]: optimization where the loads are where you have just pressure loads and how you design the holes and which material you use if you use hard

47:07.557 --> 47:17.760
[SPEAKER_01]: porsche 40 you can put more holes when you go down to the light 27 gram because it's more stretchy you have to again redesign the holes so it's

47:18.831 --> 47:30.653
[SPEAKER_01]: The more you go into the limits of the material, the more precise you are. And one also important factor is production. In 777, all our wings. From

47:30.673 --> 47:40.975
[SPEAKER_01]: the beginning, we started the 777 brand. We were maybe one of the first. All our internal construction is cut by laser. So we can play really

47:41.035 --> 47:52.575
[SPEAKER_01]: detailed with the cross holes in the ribs. We can make a really small one. We can really optimize it everywhere. but we need to use laser so all our

47:52.635 --> 48:02.718
